%description:

Tcp.windowAutoTuning:on-clamp -- when the charged segments outgrow the receive buffer, the buffer grows.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "receive window auto-tuning, as Linux (tcp_grow_window())"; Linux
tcp_clamp_window(): a buffer that the charged segments outgrow grows, up to the largest buffer.

The class on-clamp: processSegment1stThru8th() grows the receive buffer of a connection that
the application owns when the charge of its segments is above the buffer and the buffer is
below receiveBufferMax. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "on" from "off", where the buffer keeps its
size.

Host under test: host2, with a receive buffer of 16384 bytes and an advertised window of 16384
bytes (preconditions), whose TcpTestApp listens at the port 1000 and reads nothing, so the
received segments stay charged; host1 sends 100000 bytes at 0.2 s. Observation: level 3, the
receive buffer of host2 is larger than 16384 bytes at 1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowAutoTuning
%# class: on-clamp
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpWindowAutoTuningOnClamp")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(1.0)
                 .describe("the receive buffer of host2 at 1 s")
                 .assertModule("host2.tcp.conn-*", "state.rcvBufferSize > 16384"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowAutoTuningOnClamp compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 16384
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize = 16384B
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpWindowAutoTuningOnClamp: PASS
